    "result_text": "All 45 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so the `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>` and everything derived from it follows the new identity.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n- Replaced the old `nextCustomerCode(city, lastName)` (which produced `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` with a per-city sequence) with:\n  - `deriveRegion(city, postcode)` \u2014 the shared region derivation: postcode range first (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099), falling back to the city-to-region table, else `\"UNKNOWN\"`.\n  - `customerCodeFor(region, normalizedTelephone, lastName)` \u2014 builds `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, where `HASH8` is the first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName`. No sequence numbers.\n  - `sha256HexPrefix(value, hexChars)` helper.\n- In `addOwner`, the code is now built from the derived region and the already-normalized telephone.\n\nBecause the membership number (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`) and the audit line already read `customerCode`, they automatically carry the new region-and-hash identity \u2014 no further change needed.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`**\n- `deriveCheckDigit` already computes the Luhn digit over the `customerCode` digits, so it now operates on the hash-derived code automatically.\n- `deriveLocality` now reads the `REGION` prefix directly from the `customerCode` (the segment before the first `-`), so locality is derived from the new identity. It keeps the postcode-then-city fallback for owners that have no `customerCode`, preserving prior behaviour there.\n\nThe affected acceptance checkpoints (Cp09, Cp14, Cp16, Cp17, Cp21, Cp30, Cp31, Cp32, plus membership-level tests) and the full suite are all green.",
